---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import LegacyHeader from '../components/LegacyHeader.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactSection from '../components/ContactSection.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ButtonPrimary from '../components/ButtonPrimary.astro';
import ButtonSecondary from '../components/ButtonSecondary.astro';
const canonical='https://brightforge.com.ph/seo-services-new-zealand/';
const faqs=[
 {question:'Are you based in New Zealand?',answer:'No. We are based in the Philippines and deliver SEO remotely for New Zealand businesses. Manila is four hours behind New Zealand in winter and five in summer, so our morning is your afternoon. We agree access, meeting windows and review responsibilities before work starts, and we never present a remote delivery team as a local office.'},
 {question:'Can you work on an Australian and New Zealand store together?',answer:'Yes. We review which market each storefront or section serves, then check product availability, country-specific content, canonical URLs, regional alternate tags and internal links. Australian and New Zealand search performance are measured separately, so the two countries are never reported as one campaign.'},
 {question:'What are your office hours in New Zealand time?',answer:'Our office hours are Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 18:00 Manila time. Manila is UTC+8 with no daylight saving, so that is 13:00 to 22:00 in New Zealand on standard time and 14:00 to 23:00 during daylight saving. Your afternoon overlaps with our morning. We agree a meeting window inside that overlap and send written handovers for anything raised outside it.'},
 {question:'Who does the work on a New Zealand campaign?',answer:'Our own team in Quezon City. Ben Lowe, our founder, has worked in SEO for more than 15 years and leads the strategy on client work. Jani A. Cañonero is Head of Team and Jewe O. Manalo is an SEO Expert. Their profiles are on our about page. The proposal names your review contact on our side and yours.'},
 {question:'What would an NZ SEO proposal include?',answer:'The pages and searches that matter to your business, the initial technical and content priorities, responsibilities, review points and measurement. The proposal confirms the quote currency, including any NZD requirement, and the agreed scope before work starts. There is no standard price that fits every catalogue or service area.'},
 {question:'Can you improve local search visibility without being based here?',answer:'Yes, within limits. We can work on your service pages, site structure and local search information remotely. Business Profile eligibility and proximity still depend on your actual business and service area. We do not create locations or claim addresses you do not operate from.'},
 {question:'How will we know whether the campaign is working?',answer:'We separate New Zealand search impressions and clicks from other countries in Search Console and track agreed queries in New Zealand results. Enquiries or sales are included where reliable tracking is available. Each report shows completed work and the next priorities alongside the results. Rankings and time frames are not guaranteed.'}
];
const service={ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Service',name:'SEO Services for New Zealand Businesses',serviceType:'Search engine optimisation',url:canonical,areaServed:{'@type':'Country',name:'New Zealand'},provider:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Bright Forge SEO',url:'https://brightforge.com.ph/'},description:'Technical, ecommerce and content SEO for New Zealand businesses, delivered remotely from the Philippines.'};
---
<MainLayout title="SEO Services for New Zealand Businesses | Bright Forge" description="SEO for New Zealand businesses from our Philippines team, with a published NZ ecommerce case study, separate NZ reporting and proposals in NZD where agreed." canonical={canonical} type="service" faqs={faqs} geoRegion="NZ" geoPlacename="New Zealand" contentLanguage="en-NZ">
  <Fragment slot="head"><script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(service)} /></Fragment>
  <LegacyHeader slot="header" />
  <Hero badgeIcon="fas fa-globe" badgeText="SEO for New Zealand Businesses" title="SEO for New Zealand Businesses, <span>Grounded in Your Market</span>" breadcrumbCurrent="SEO Services New Zealand">
    <Fragment slot="story">
      <p>New Zealand is often handled as an afterthought to an Australian campaign. Your New Zealand customers do not necessarily search, compare or buy like Australian customers, so we treat New Zealand as its own market: its own keyword research, its own competitors and its own report, built around the products you sell here and the places you serve.</p>
      <p>We deliver from the Philippines, with agreed review windows and a scope set out in a written proposal. Our published Speediance New Zealand case study shows a separate campaign on a real NZ storefront, with its own keyword mapping rather than Australian pages with the country name changed.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="actions"><ButtonPrimary href="/contact/" text="Discuss Your NZ Website" /><ButtonSecondary href="#nz-proof" text="See New Zealand Work" /></Fragment>
  </Hero>
  <section class="nz-section" id="nz-proof">
    <div class="nz-wrap nz-split">
      <div><p class="nz-eyebrow">Published New Zealand Work</p><h2>Speediance New Zealand: <span>Organic Clicks From 927 to 2,570 in Six Months</span></h2><p>Speediance New Zealand (speediance.nz) competes for smart home gym demand with the same core product family as the brand's other regional shops. We mapped commercial and consumer search intent across NZ, improved product and category content, worked on the technical side of the store and built relevant authority.</p><p>Over six months, compared with the previous six, the published case study reports Search Console clicks rising from 927 to 2,570, impressions from 46,600 to 85,800 and average position improving from 31.3 to 25.0. These are site-wide search figures for the NZ storefront. They do not measure orders, and the comparison does not isolate the effect of any one tactic. It is one campaign result, not a forecast for another site.</p><a href="/case-studies/speediance-nz-fitness-seo/">Read the Speediance NZ case study</a></div>
      <aside class="nz-proof"><span>Published Six-Month Comparison</span><strong>927 to 2,570</strong><p>Organic search clicks in the case study.</p><p>We assess your starting point and competition before recommending a scope. A past result does not set your delivery date or likely return.</p></aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="pf-section" id="nz-agency-or-philippines-team">
    <div class="pf-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Choosing a supplier</p>
      <h2>A New Zealand agency or <span>a Philippines team</span>: the trade-offs</h2>
      <p class="pf-lede">Both can do good work. The differences are practical, and you should weigh them against how your business likes to work.</p>
      <div class="pf-table-wrap"><table class="pf-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Agency in New Zealand</th><th scope="col" class="pf-us">Bright Forge, from the Philippines</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Working hours</th><td>Your business day, in your time zone.</td><td class="pf-us">13:00 to 22:00 NZST, or 14:00 to 23:00 NZDT. Your afternoon is our morning.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Meetings</th><td>Face to face is possible.</td><td class="pf-us">Video calls in an agreed window, run from our team in Quezon City.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Local presence</th><td>A local address and local staff.</td><td class="pf-us">Remote delivery from the Philippines. Local search rests on your own premises and service area, whichever agency you hire.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">NZ evidence</th><td>Ask for published work on a New Zealand site, with dated figures.</td><td class="pf-us">A published six-month case on speediance.nz: organic clicks from 927 to 2,570.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Reporting</th><td>Ask whether NZ and Australian results are reported separately.</td><td class="pf-us">Country-filtered Search Console data and NZ-specific queries, reported on their own.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Quote currency</th><td>NZD.</td><td class="pf-us">Stated in the written proposal, in NZD where agreed.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p class="pf-note">Hours are converted from our published office hours, Monday to Friday, 9:00 to 18:00 Manila time (UTC+8, no daylight saving).</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="nz-section nz-muted">
    <div class="nz-wrap"><p class="nz-eyebrow">Four Starting Points</p><h2>NZ SEO for Stores, Service Firms and Agencies: <span>Where Each One Starts</span></h2>
      <div class="nz-row"><h3>NZ Ecommerce Stores</h3><div><p>We separate collection searches from product searches, review how out-of-stock and discontinued products are handled, and check that regional storefronts send shoppers and search engines to the correct version. Product availability, delivery information and buyer language must match the NZ offer, in New Zealand English.</p><a href="/ecommerce-seo-services/">Explore ecommerce SEO</a></div></div>
      <div class="nz-row"><h3>Service Businesses</h3><div><p>We start with your real service areas and the jobs you want to win. Existing service pages often need clearer scope, proof or enquiry paths before another location page is worth writing. Local campaigns rest on your actual business location and eligibility. An agency claiming to be nearby adds nothing to either.</p><a href="/local-seo-for-google-maps-and-gbp/">See our local SEO approach</a></div></div>
      <div class="nz-row"><h3>Sites With Technical Obstacles</h3><div><p>We identify which valuable pages are blocked, duplicated or difficult to crawl, then separate implementation defects from normal search-processing delays. Every recommendation names the affected URLs, the proposed change and how the result will be checked.</p><a href="/technical-seo-services-philippines/">Review technical SEO support</a></div></div>
      <div class="nz-row"><h3>Agencies Needing Delivery Support</h3><div><p>We agree which parts of strategy, implementation and reporting sit with your agency. Work can be prepared under your brand, with named review points and a clear boundary around client communication. You retain the client relationship.</p><a href="/white-label-seo-services-philippines/">Discuss white-label fulfilment</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="nz-section"><div class="nz-wrap nz-split"><div><p class="nz-eyebrow">New Zealand Is Its Own Market</p><h2>NZ and Australian Search Performance, <span>Measured and Reported Separately</span></h2><p>If you operate both storefronts, we check what belongs to each one before changing URLs or regional tags. Shared products do not make the pages interchangeable: stock, shipping, currency and customer questions can differ.</p><p>We compare country-filtered Search Console data and agreed country-specific queries. That stops Australian exposure, or a branded search from another country, being counted as new NZ demand, and it stops growth in one store masking a decline in the other.</p><p>For a coordinated campaign, see our <a href="/seo-services-australia/">Australian SEO services</a>. If one website serves several countries, our <a href="/international-seo-services/">international SEO service</a> covers the structure and regional tags. For a redesign or store move, involve <a href="/website-migration-services/">migration SEO support</a> before new URLs are locked in.</p></div><aside class="nz-proof"><h3>What We Need From You</h3><ul><li>Your website and the products or services that matter most.</li><li>The locations you genuinely serve and any separate regional stores.</li><li>Relevant Search Console access and reliable enquiry or sales measurement.</li><li>Your review contact, implementation resources and planned launch dates.</li></ul><p>We confirm meeting windows around NZ daylight-saving changes and state the quote currency, including NZD where agreed, in the proposal.</p></aside></div></section>
  <section class="nz-section nz-muted"><div class="nz-wrap"><p class="nz-eyebrow">A Defined First Engagement</p><h2>The First Engagement: <span>Diagnosis, Priorities and a Handover You Can Check</span></h2><p>We begin by comparing your important pages with the businesses that appear for the searches you want. The first recommendations tell you which searches have no page at all and which have a page that needs improving. Where the cause of weak visibility is not yet clear, an <a href="/seo-audit-services/">SEO audit</a> is the right starting point.</p><p>Agreed work lists its target URLs, its dependencies and its acceptance checks. Reporting separates completed changes, search performance and outstanding decisions. You will not receive a long activity list in place of evidence that the intended page or fix is live.</p></div></section>
  <section class="pf-section" id="nz-how-to-start">
    <div class="pf-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How to start</p>
      <h2>Three steps from <span>first message to agreed scope</span></h2>
      <p class="pf-lede">Nothing is changed on your site until the scope is agreed in writing.</p>
      <ol class="pf-steps">
        <li><strong>Send us the site</strong><span>Your website, the products or services that matter most, the places you serve and any separate regional stores. We usually reply within one business day.</span></li>
        <li><strong>We review and talk it through</strong><span>We compare your important pages with the businesses that appear for the searches you want, in New Zealand results, and agree a meeting window in your afternoon.</span></li>
        <li><strong>You receive a written proposal</strong><span>It sets out the first priorities, responsibilities, review points, measurement and the quote currency. Work starts once you approve it.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="nz-section"><div class="nz-wrap"><h2>Questions About <span>SEO Delivery for New Zealand</span></h2><div class="nz-faqs">{faqs.map(f=><details><summary>{f.question}</summary><p>{f.answer}</p></details>)}</div><div class="nz-actions"><ButtonPrimary href="/contact/" text="Discuss Your New Zealand Campaign" /><ButtonSecondary href="/case-studies/" text="Review Published Work" /></div></div></section>
  <ContactSection slot="contact" /><Footer slot="footer" />
</MainLayout>
<style>
.nz-section{padding:clamp(3rem,6vw,6rem) 0;background:#ffffff;color:#465365}.nz-muted{background:#ffffff}.nz-wrap{width:min(1120px,calc(100% - 2.5rem));margin-inline:auto}.nz-split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1fr;gap:3rem;align-items:start}.nz-eyebrow{color:#b83e12;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:700;font-size:.8rem}.nz-section h2{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3.4vw,2.8rem);font-weight:800;color:#19212e;line-height:1.15;margin:.6rem 0 1.6rem}.nz-section h2 span{color:#b83e12}.nz-section h3{font-size:1.3rem;color:#19212e;font-weight:700}.nz-section p{line-height:1.8;margin:1rem 0}.nz-section a:not(:global(.btn-primary)):not(:global(.btn-secondary)){color:#b83e12;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.2em}.nz-proof{padding:2rem;border:1px solid #ffffff20;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f7f8fa,#f7f8fa);border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 12px 35px #0003}.nz-proof strong{display:block;font-size:clamp(1.9rem,3vw,2.7rem);color:#19212e;margin:.8rem 0}.nz-proof span{color:#b83e12;font-size:.8rem;text-transform:uppercase}.nz-proof ul{padding-left:1.2rem;line-height:1.9}.nz-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;gap:2rem;padding:1.8rem 0;border-top:1px solid #ffffff20}.nz-row p{margin-top:0}.nz-faqs details{border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff25;padding:1.2rem 0}.nz-faqs summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;color:#19212e;line-height:1.5}.nz-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;margin-top:2rem}@media(max-width:760px){.nz-split,.nz-row{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.3rem}.nz-proof{padding:1.4rem}.nz-wrap{width:calc(100% - 2rem)}}
</style>
